                <pb facs="0551" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg471"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Storer to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Storer acknowledges receipt of the Department’s telegram of May 10, in
                    regard to the Filipino junta, and reports that the matter is receiving his
                    particular attention; that up to the present time trustworthy information has
                    been difficult to obtain, and that he is of the opinion that something of no
                    consequence has been exaggerated by newspaper reports.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
